# Retired pages -> closest live equivalent. These must sit above the SPA
# fallback: Netlify matches _redirects rules in order, and a catch-all below
# would otherwise answer with index.html and a 200 (a soft 404).
/services/move-in-assembly    /services/furniture-assembly   301!

# SPA fallback, scoped to the route families that are deliberately NOT
# pre-rendered (see ssgOptions.includedRoutes in vite.config.ts). Every public
# page ships as a real .html file in dist and Netlify serves it directly, so no
# public URL belongs in this list.
#
# This was a blanket `/*  /index.html  200`, which answered EVERY unknown URL
# with the homepage shell at HTTP 200. Google reads that as a real page and
# indexes the junk as a duplicate of the homepage, then keeps re-crawling it;
# it also hid missing JS chunks and loader JSON behind HTML instead of a 404.
# Unmatched paths now fall through to dist/404.html, which Netlify serves with
# a real 404 status.
#
# Netlify ignores trailing slashes when matching, so `/admin` covers `/admin/`.
/admin       /index.html   200
/admin/*     /index.html   200
/portal      /index.html   200
/portal/*    /index.html   200
/book        /index.html   200
/go/*        /index.html   200
/pay/*       /index.html   200
